---
import { u } from '../lib/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { t } from '../i18n/en';
import { getData } from '../lib/data';
const { claims, indices, series } = getData();
---
<Base title={t.data.title}>
  <h1>{t.data.title}</h1>
  <p>The whole site is generated from plain JSON files: one file per claim, plus index rankings and time series. This build contains <strong>{claims.length}</strong> claims, <strong>{indices.length}</strong> indices and <strong>{series.length}</strong> series.</p>
  <p>The merged claims file includes every claim, including drafts (see the <code>review_status</code> field). Fields follow the project schema: speaker, date, venue, quote_original, quote_english, quote_is_verbatim, claim_type, deadline, verdict, summary, topics, media, evidence, govt_response, analysis, confidence, review_status, last_reviewed, notes.</p>
  <p>
    <a href={u('/downloads/claims.json')} download><button type="button">{t.data.downloadJson}</button></a>
    <a href={u('/downloads/claims.csv')} download><button type="button">{t.data.downloadCsv}</button></a>
  </p>
  <p class="sans small muted">CSV flattens lists: topics and URLs are joined with “ | ”. Use the JSON for full detail.</p>
</Base>
